{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274691-questions-about-momentum","id":1274691,"title":"Questions about Momentum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-16T05:09:23-08:00","id":1274691,"title":"Questions about Momentum","content":"1) Do you start the game sessions with Momentum? How many, in that case?<br /> 2) Do Momentum go away after a session or campaign or whatever?<br /> 3) Do you have to spend Momentum BEFORE a roll or can you do it after you've seen the result of a normal roll?<br /> 4) If you fail a roll that you spent Momentum on, do you still get more Momentum as consolation?<br /> <br /> From what I've seen there's about 40% chance to actually get a response to rules-related questions here, but I hope this is a good day since I can't seem to find any of this in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T11:42:03-08:00","id":1274746,"title":"","content":"1 - It doesn\u2019t appear so. <br /> 2 - I\u2019d carry it over between sessions and reset between campaigns. <br /> 3 - p.72 implies that you can spend momentum after seeing a roll\u2019s results. &quot;If the Difficulty is too high for the number of successes a player has, he can choose to spend Momentum or fail and take a Consolation. These are covered in greater detail on p. XX.&quot;<br /> 4 - Can\u2019t find anything that says you don\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T21:11:22-08:00","id":1274830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274691-questions-about-momentum?p=1274746#post1274746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - It doesn\u2019t appear so.<br /> 2 - I\u2019d carry it over between sessions and reset between campaigns.<br /> 3 - p.72 implies that you can spend momentum after seeing a roll\u2019s results. &quot;If the Difficulty is too high for the number of successes a player has, he can choose to spend Momentum or fail and take a Consolation. These are covered in greater detail on p. XX.&quot;<br /> 4 - Can\u2019t find anything that says you don\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, thanks! Seems like I interpreted the rules correctly then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":